<title>AUSTRALIA: Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - August 4.</title>
<headline>Highest/Lowest Australian P-E Ratios - August 4.</headline>
<dateline>SYDNEY 1996-08-04</dateline>
<text>
<p>Highest and lowest price earnings ratios for Australian companies included in the 320-company All Ordinaries Index based on closing prices on Friday. P/E based on rolling 12 months earnings.</p>
<p>Highest 10 Rank Name		     P/E    Close</p>
<p> 1   Mayne Nickless	 386.14   7.80</p>
<p> 2   Ranger Minerals	185.10   3.85</p>
<p> 3   Syd Hrbr Casino	177.69   2.15</p>
<p> 4   Perilya Mines	  126.83   0.52</p>
<p> 5   Westpac Prop Tr	112.50   1.80</p>
<p> 6   Tap Oil		   93.75   1.65</p>
<p> 7   Bougainville	    89.06   0.57</p>
<p> 8   Consol Paper	    82.35   2.80</p>
<p> 9   Oil Search		80.15   4.16</p>
<p>10   Computershare	   79.71  14.10</p>
<p>Lowest 10  1   Climax Mining	    1.51   0.75</p>
<p> 2   Consol Rutile	    3.66   0.82</p>
<p> 3   Jardine Fm China	 5.67   0.84</p>
<p> 4   Haoma Mining	     6.07   0.30</p>
<p> 5   Renison Goldflds	 6.11   4.16</p>
<p> 6   Mt Leyshon Gold	  6.67   1.55</p>
